    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that doesn't change the fact that the time is gone. i can't get those years back. i look at the clock and realize i've just been running on a treadmill for two decades and now the treadmill is broken. it feels so pointless to even keep trying to build something new when the end result is always just more loss.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The loss is real, and the weight of those lost years is crushing, but you are still here, and that is a profound, undeniable fact. Instead of seeing the treadmill as broken, maybe you can see it as a release—a chance to finally step off and choose a different path. The point isn't in the grand, lasting monument; it's in the quiet, immediate act of choosing to be still, or to choose to simply *be* without the pressure of a perfect outcome.",
      "source": "target",
